00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:07,280
"“Well,, doing homework together is a good thing,”." Ms. Reuben answered,, "“but you’re

224
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:10,560
supposed to still do it separately,, okay??

225
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:14,760
You could work side by side if you want,, but you can’t actually do your homework

226
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:16,760
together,, okay??

227
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:18,400
Got it?”?"

228
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:23,480
After we left the classroom,, I said:, "“Dude,, thanks for doing that.”."

229
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:26,400
And he was like,, "“No problem.”."

230
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:28,080
That was cool..

231
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:34,160
Fourthly,, now that I know him,, I would say I actually do want to be friends with August..

232
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:38,440
At first, I'll admit it,, I was only friendly to him because Mr.. Tushman

233
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:41,400
asked me to be especially nice and all that..

234
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:44,040
But now I would choose to hang out with him..

235
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:48,880
He laughs at all my jokes., And I kind of feel like I can tell August anything..

236
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:53,440
Like, he’s a good friend.. Like,, if all the guys in the fifth grade were lined

237
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:57,680
up against a wall and I got to choose anyone I wanted to hang out with,,

238
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:00,880
I would choose August.

239
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:06,000
Ex-Friends BLEEDING SCREAM? "WHAT the heck??"

240
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:10,880
Summer Dawson has always been a bit out there,, but this was too much..

241
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:15,760
All I did was ask her why August was acting like he was mad at me or something..

242
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:17,720
I figured she would know..

243
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:20,560
And all she said was, "“Bleeding Scream”?."

244
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:23,240
I don’t even know what that means..

245
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:27,400
It’s so weird because one day, me and August were friends.

246
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:31,520
And the next day,, whoosh,, he was hardly talking to me..

247
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:34,360
And I haven’t the slightest idea why..

248
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:39,040
When I said to him,, "“Hey, August,, you mad at me or something?”?"

249
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:41,120
he shrugged and walked away..

250
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:44,200
So, I would take that as a definite yes..

251
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:47,800
And since I know for a fact that I didn’t do anything to him to be mad

252
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:51,680
about,, I figured Summer could tell me what’s up..

253
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:55,040
But all I got from her was “Bleeding Scream”?.

254
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:58,240
Yeah,, big help.. Thanks,, Summer..

255
00:15:58,240 --> 00:16:02,120
You know,, I’ve got plenty of other friends in school.. So, if August wants

256
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:08,200
to officially be my ex-friend,, then fine,. that is okay by me,. see if I care..

257
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:11,880
I’ve started ignoring him like he’s ignoring me in school now..

258
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:15,720
This is actually kind of hard since we sit next to each other in practically

259
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:20,440
every class.. Other kids have noticed and have started asking me if me and August

260
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,080
have had a fight..

261
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,800
Nobody asked August what’s going on..

262
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:27,280
Hardly anyone ever talks to him, anyway..

263
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:32,640
I mean,, the only person he hangs out with, other than me, is Summer..

264
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:36,720
Sometimes he hangs out with Reed Kingsley a little bit, and the two Maxes

265
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:41,600
got him playing Dungeons and Dragons a couple of times at recess..

266
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:45,280
Charlotte,, for all her goody-two-shoeing, doesn’t ever do more

267
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:48,320
than nod hello when she’s passing him in the hallway..

268
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:52,240
And I don’t know if everyone’s still playing the Plague behind his back,

269
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:55,960
because no one ever really told me about it directly,,

270
00:16:55,960 --> 00:17:00,240
but my point is that it’s not like he has a whole lot of other friends he

271
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:03,040
could be hanging out with instead of me..

272
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:08,640
If he wants to diss me,, he’s the one who loses—, —not me..

273
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:11,560
So, this is how things are between us now..

274
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:15,800
We only talk to each other about school stuff if we absolutely have to..

275
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:19,600
Like, I’ll say,, "“What did Reuben say the homework was?”?"

276
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:21,000
and he’ll answer..

277
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,560
Or he’ll be like,, "“Can I use your pencil sharpener?”?"

278
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:27,720
and I’ll get my sharpener out of my pencil case for him..

279
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:32,000
But as soon as the bell rings,, we go our separate ways..

280
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Why this is good is because I get to hang out a lot more with kids now..

281
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:42,680
Before,, when I was hanging out with August all the time,, kids weren’t hanging out with me

282
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:44,880
cuz they’d have to hang out with him..

283
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:48,800
Or they would keep things from me,, like the whole thing about the Plague..

284
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,720
I think I was the only one who wasn’t in

285
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:56,480
on it,, except for Summer and maybe the D&&&D crowd.. And the truth is,,

286
00:17:56,480 --> 00:18:01,480
though nobody’s that obvious about it:, nobody wants to hang out with him..

287
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:06,360
Everyone’s way too hung up on being in the popular group,, and he’s just as far

288
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:09,240
from the popular group as you can get..

289
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:11,000
But now that I can hang out with anyone

290
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:15,920
I want., If I wanted to be in the popular group,, I could totally be in the popular

291
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:22,200
group.. Why this is bad is because,, well,, (a), I don’t actually enjoy hanging out with

292
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:28,000
the popular group that much., And (b), I actually liked hanging out with August..

293
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:33,880
So, this is kind of messed up., And it’s all August’s fault.

294
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:35,360
Snow.

295
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:39,160
THE FIRST SNOW of winter hit right before Thanksgiving break.. School was

296
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:43,440
closed, and we got an extra day of vacation.. I was glad about that because

297
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:47,480
I was so bummed about this whole August thing, and I just wanted some time to

298
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:50,080
chill without having to see him every day..

299
00:18:50,080 --> 00:18:55,280
Also,, waking up to a snow day is just about my favorite thing in the world..

300
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:58,520
I love that feeling when you first open your eyes in the morning, and you don’t

301
00:18:58,520 --> 00:19:01,760
even know why everything seems different than usual..

302
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:03,200
Then it hits you:.

303
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:04,960
Everything is quiet..

304
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:10,320
No cars honking.. No buses going down the street.. Then you run over to the window,,

305
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:15,000
and outside everything is covered in white:. the sidewalks,, the trees,, the

306
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:18,280
cars on the street,, your window panes.

307
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:22,840
And when that happens on a school day and you find out your school is closed,,

308
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:25,680
well,, I don’t care how old I get:, I’m

309
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:29,960
always going to think that that’s the best feeling in the world.. And I’m never

310
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:33,920
going to be one of those grown-ups that use an umbrella when it’s snowing—.

311
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:38,560
—ever.. Dad’s school was closed,, too,. so, he took me and Jamie sledding down

312
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:40,680
Skeleton Hill in the park..

313
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:45,440
They say a little kid broke his neck while sledding down that hill a few years ago,,

314
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:50,000
but I don’t know if this is actually true or just one of those legends..

315
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:54,120
On the way home,, I spotted this banged-up wooden sled kind of propped up

316
00:19:54,120 --> 00:19:56,920
against the Old Indian Rock monument..

317
00:19:56,920 --> 00:20:00,120
Dad said to leave it,. it was just garbage,.

318
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:03,600
but something told me it would make the greatest sled ever..

319
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:06,600
So, Dad let me drag it home,. and I spent

320
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:11,440
the rest of the day fixing it up.. I superglued the broken slats together and

321
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:15,480
wrapped some heavy-duty duct tape around them for extra strength. And I

322
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:19,480
spray-painted the whole thing white with the paint I had gotten for the Alabaster

323
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:23,160
Sphinx I was making for the Egyptian Museum project..

324
00:20:23,160 --> 00:20:28,720
When it was all dry,, I painted LIGHTNING in gold letters on the middle pieces of wood,.

325
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:32,200
and I made a little lightning bolt system above the letters..

326
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:35,040
It looked pretty professional,, I have to say..

327
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:39,480
Dad was like,, "“Wow,, Jackie!. You were right about the sled!”."

328
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:43,280
The next day,, we went back to Hill with Lightning.

329
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:45,800
It was the fastest thing I'd ever ridden—.

330
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:50,360
—so,, so,, so much faster than the plastic sleds we’d been using..

331
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:55,640
And because it had gotten warmer outside,, the snow had become crunchier and wetter:.

332
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:57,280
good packing snow..

333
00:20:57,280 --> 00:21:00,480
Me and Jamie took turns on Lightning all afternoon..

334
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:04,960
We were in the park until our fingers were frozen and our lips had turned a little blue..

335
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:07,760
Dad practically had to drag us home..

336
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:11,520
By the end of the weekend,, the snow had started turning gray and yellow,, and

337
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:14,960
then a rainstorm turned most of the snow to slush..

338
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:18,600
When we got back to school on Monday,, there was no snow left..

339
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:23,600
It was rainy and yucky the first day back from vacation., A slushy day.. That’s

340
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:26,280
how I was feeling inside,, too..

341
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:31,080
I nodded “hey” to August the first time I saw him.. We were in front of the lockers..

342
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:33,000
He nodded “hey” back..

343
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:38,320
I wanted to tell him about Lightning, but I didn’t.

344
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:43,200
Thank you for watching. Please like and subscribe. Become a channel member, and

345
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:46,360
we'll see you next time.
